+*   **Strengths:** Flexible kernel formulation allows for arbitrary pattern shapes; suitable for structured texture synthesis [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** For high curvature or vorticity, the spots tend to blur out the flow structure [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Spot noise was introduced by van Wijk [vW91] and further developed by de Lavergtelle et al. [dLvL97] as a sparse convolution noise method [Lew89]. It is based on the idea of developing a pattern after many thousands of tiny drops, representing a flow field [S1, unofficial]. The method has been used in volumetric texture synthesis and flow visualization [S2, unofficial].
+Spot noise was introduced by van Wijk [vW91] and further developed by de Lavergtelle et al. [dLvL97] as a sparse convolution noise method [Lew89]. It is based on the idea of developing a pattern after many thousands of tiny drops, representing a flow field [S1, unofficial]. The method is defined as a sparse convolution noise with a flexible kernel formulation where a uniform distribution of impulses is convolved with an arbitrary kernel spatially defined [S2, unofficial].
 
